#' Synthetic multi-donor count data for scRoPE teaching examples
#'
#' Eight genes and 1,200 cells from 30 independent simulated donors, with
#' 40 cells per donor. The first 20 donors are controls and the last 10 treated.
#' These are artificial teaching data, not biological or paper-analysis data.
#'
#' @source Generated by the package's reproducible synthetic-example scripts,
#' with seed 20261020 and the specification in
#' \code{system.file("examples", "synthetic_parameters.R", package="scRoPE")}.
#' @details The reference generator uses mean-one gamma donor effects with
#' variance 0.12 and conditional negative-binomial counts with dispersion 0.25.
#' X1 is a standard-normal cell predictor, X2 is the donor treatment indicator,
#' and cc is a balanced artificial cell category with case as reference.
#' Treatment coefficients for G01--G08 are -0.6, -0.3, 0, 0, 0, 0.3, 0.6, 0.9.
#' Supply the provided multiplicative offsets when fitting. The companion
#' generator also creates a paired lognormal-donor illustration. A single
#' realization does not establish calibration or power. Historical inherited
#' examples remain in historical sources; this maintained object replaces them.
#'
#' @format A list of four objects:
#' \describe{
#'   \item{count}{An 8 by 1,200 sparse matrix of nonnegative integer counts.}
#'   \item{sid}{Donor IDs D01--D30, contiguous in blocks of 40 cells.}
#'   \item{pred}{A data frame with X1, X2 and cc, in count-column order.}
#'   \item{offset}{Positive multiplicative cell scaling factors.}
#' }
#' @usage data(sample_data)
"sample_data"

#' Matching synthetic Seurat teaching object
#'
#' A Seurat object containing exactly the counts and cells in \code{sample_data}:
#' eight genes and 1,200 cells. No real human data are included.
#'
#' @source Constructed from the package's synthetic \code{sample_data} using
#' \code{make_synthetic_seurat()} in the installed examples generator.
#' @details The RNA assay contains the reference count matrix. Metadata include
#' X1, X2, cc and offset, with replicate equal to sid. Compatibility labels
#' celltype (equal to cc) and tech (synthetic_control/synthetic_treatment)
#' are artificial, not measured cell types or sequencing technologies.
#' Use \code{scToNeb(sample_seurat, assay="RNA", id="replicate",
#' pred=c("X1", "X2", "cc"), offset="offset")} for the matching inputs.
#'
#' @format A Seurat object with an RNA count assay and per-cell metadata.
#' @usage data(sample_seurat)
"sample_seurat"
